      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1874 the Allegheny Car & Transportation Shops opened, later bought by George Westinghouse, who founded Union Switch & Signal right here.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swissvale%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Radio pioneer Frank Conrad lived in Swissvale from 1910‑15 and conducted early transmission experiments that helped launch KDKA, the world’s first commercial radio station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swissvale%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Swissvale sits just 9 miles east of downtown Pittsburgh, overlooking the Monongahela River Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swissvale%2C_Pennsylvania",
